Xray-core: add the backend's stability penalty to a door's score

The autoselect outbound (xray-autoselect.patch) sends new connections to
the member with the lowest score: median probe delay + 0.5 x jitter
+ 800 x the share of recent connections that failed, + 1500 while suspect
and + 150 when its numbers are stale. Member order only breaks exact ties.
A probe shows whether a door answers. It does not show whether the door
keeps working for the length of a session.

On some networks, Cloudflare (CDN) doors answer probes fast but fail in
the middle of sessions far more often than IPv6 Reality doors. The core
kept choosing the CDN doors, and phones spent much of their mobile time on
them.

A new "penalties" setting maps member tags to milliseconds added to the
member's score. The backend measures each door across phones and sends
its penalty with the door (penalty_ms in /api/v1/configs/dedicated). The
app writes the doors with a penalty above 0 into this setting.

- It is added only to a ranked member. A dead or never measured member
  stays unranked, so a penalty never makes a dead door win, and a door
  that is the only one working is used whatever its penalty.
- Failover targets and the order a failed connection is retried in come
  from the same score, so they follow it too.
- Tags the group does not hold, and values of 0 or less, are ignored.
- The status reports each member's penaltyMs. Its score includes it.

